{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nThe blue-green autodeploy of the `mcp` target is crash-looping on a fail-closed auth check, and\nthe box is currently serving a **hand-patched container whose fix is not in git**. The next\nsuccessful deploy will revert that patch and re-break the service.\n\n`rebar-autodeploy-errors` is IN ALARM (confirmed 2026-08-25 via `describe-alarms`, us-east-1).\n\n## Evidence\n\nVerbatim from SSM invocation `0d3b8b4b` (2026-08-25T16:37:45Z):\n\n    rebar._mcp_auth.AuthConfigError: static tokens file '/run/secrets/mcp-static-tokens.json' defines no tokens\n      File \"/app/src/rebar/mcp_server.py\", line 774, in main\n        server = build_server(cfg)\n      File \"/app/src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py\", line 725, in _load_static_tokens\n\nThis is the documented fail-closed posture at `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:367-371`.\n\nConsequence, from invocation `448230fe`:\n\n    AUTODEPLOY_ERROR {\"reason\": \"mcp-unhealthy\", \"detail\": \"new mcp container rebar-mcp-d49466b5e960-8092 failed /health within 120s; removing it, leaving the OLD upstream live\"}\n    AUTODEPLOY_ERROR {\"reason\": \"deploy_failed\", \"detail\": \"target=d49466b5e960... fail#9 backoff=900s\"}\n\nAn operator recovered manually at 16:55Z by injecting `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL` via `env_file`\nand running `compose recreate` (invocation `d1d2ce4a` — \"HEALTHY at t=8\",\n\"Uvicorn running on http://0.0.0.0:8091\"). A live probe confirms\n`GET https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` returns `HTTP 401 invalid_token`, so it is serving.\n\n## Why this is urgent\n\n1. The running config is out-of-band. The `env_file` injection is not committed, so it is one\n   successful autodeploy away from being lost.\n2. The deployed code is stale: the box serves `d49466b5e960`, four commits behind `main` HEAD at\n   the time of investigation.\n3. `fail#9 backoff=900s` means the loop is still retrying and still failing.\n\nThis is INDEPENDENT of the missing-tickets-store defect — it explains why the deployed code is\nstale, not why `fsck` reports an uninitialized store. Neither causes the other.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (REVISED — the original set rested on a premise since retracted)\n\nThe original AC1 asked that \"the operator's manual REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL fix be captured in\ngit so a deploy reproduces it rather than reverting it\". That criterion is VOID: the value was\nalready supplied from git by BOTH `docker-compose.yml` and `mcp_run_new`, each with the same\ndefault, and `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py` already pinned it. The operator's hand-added\n`.env` line was redundant, not load-bearing, and there was nothing to capture. See the\n\"CORRECTION #2\" comment. Ticking it would have claimed work that was never needed.\n\nThe real, single defect and its criteria:\n\n- [x] The mcp blue-green deploy path re-materializes its SSM-sourced secrets before starting the\n      replacement container, so a rotated credential reaches it without a manual operator run.\n      Delivered: `fetch-secrets.sh` is invoked in the mcp block of `autodeploy.sh`, before the\n      build and well before `mcp_run_new`.\n- [x] The refresh is FAIL-FAST with the same semantics as the review-bot path: an SSM error\n      aborts the deploy while the OLD container is still serving, rather than replacing a\n      working container using stale secrets. Delivered: `mcp-secrets-fetch-failed`.\n- [x] A secrets-refresh failure is distinguishable in the error signal from a generic\n      `mcp-unhealthy`. Delivered: its own named reason, asserted by\n      `test_secrets_fetch_failure_aborts_before_touching_the_live_upstream`.\n- [x] Regression coverage pins the ORDERING that makes it safe (refresh strictly before the new\n      container starts), and the structural check pins that the call exists at all:\n      `test_mcp_bluegreen_refreshes_ssm_secrets_before_starting_the_new_container`.\n- [x] `rebar-autodeploy-errors` is OK. Verified via `describe-alarms` after the merge, with\n      `rebar/host:deploy_errors` reading 0.0 across the preceding 30 minutes.\n\n## Completion evidence (merged origin/main 30d7059f632d)\n\nLanded as Gerrit 2230 with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. Both new tests were mutation-checked:\nremoving the `fetch-secrets.sh` call turns each RED, and restoring it turns them GREEN."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787727700157309001,"uuid":"e964bdb0-a646-4358-9e60-1aefa08952d8"}